Solve for \(x\), algebraically.
\[
e^{2 x+1}=5^{x}
\]

\section*{Solution}
\[
\begin{aligned}
\ln \left(e^{2 x+1}\right) & =\ln \left(5^{x}\right) & & 1 / 2 \text { mark for applying logarithms } \\
(2 x+1) \ln e & =x \ln 5 & & 1 \text { mark for power law }(1 / 2 \text { mark for each }) \\
2 x+1 & =x \ln 5 & & \\
2 x-x \ln 5 & =-1 & & 1 / 2 \text { mark for collecting terms with } x \\
x(2-\ln 5) & =-1 & &
\end{aligned}
\]
\[
\begin{aligned}
& x=\frac{-1}{2-\ln 5} \quad \frac{1}{2} \text { mark for isolating } x \\
& x=-2.560412 \ldots \\
& x=-2.560 \quad 1 / 2 \text { mark for evaluating quotient of logarithms }
\end{aligned}
\]

