Given \(f(x)=x^{3}+1\), determine the equation of \(f^{-1}(x)\).

\section*{Solution}

Let \(y=f(x)\)
\[
y=x^{3}+1
\]
To determine the inverse of \(f(x)\), switch \(x\) and \(y\).
\[
\begin{aligned}
& x=y^{3}+1 \\
& x-1=y^{3} \\
& \sqrt[3]{x-1}=y \\
& f^{-1}(x)=\sqrt[3]{x-1}
\end{aligned}
\]

