Determine all of the zeros of the function \(p(x)=x^{3}-2 x^{2}-9 x+18\).

\section*{Solution}
\[
\begin{aligned}
p(2) & =2^{3}-2(2)^{2}-9(2)+18 \quad 1 \text { mark for identifying one possible zero of } p(x) \\
& =0 \\
& \therefore(x-2) \text { is a factor of } p(x)
\end{aligned}
\]

\begin{tabular}[t]{|l|l|l|l|l|}
\hline 2 & 1 & -2 & -9 & 18 \\
\hline & & 2 & 0 & -18 \\
\hline & 1 & 0 & -9 & 0 \\
\hline
\end{tabular}

1 mark for synthetic division (or equivalent strategy)
\[
\begin{array}{ll}
(x-2)\left(x^{2}-9\right)=0 & 1 / 2 \text { mark for consistent factors } \\
(x-2)(x-3)(x+3)=0 & \\
x=2, x=3, x=-3 & 1 / 2 \text { mark for consistent zeros }
\end{array}
\]

