\section*{Solution}
\(\left(\frac{\sqrt{23}}{6}\right)^{2}+y^{2}=1 \quad \frac{1}{2}\) mark for substitution
\(\frac{23}{36}+y^{2}=1\)
\(y^{2}=\frac{36}{36}-\frac{23}{36}\)
\(y= \pm \frac{\sqrt{13}}{6} \quad 1 / 2\) mark for exact values of \(y\)
